 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "panasonic nn h98 not heating anymore, any fix?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "No, there is no simple user fix for a microwave that is not heating. This issue usually involves internal high-voltage components like the magnetron or capacitor which require professional repair. From what you have described, the most likely cause is the high-voltage heating system. Heat a cup of water for a minute on full power. Is the water hot now, or still cold?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "tried a cup of water, stops after about 10-15 seconds with H98 and the water's still cold. H98 is what the screen says when it stops, the model on the back is NN-CD87KSBPQ"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "H98 on your Panasonic means: Magnetron/HV inverter power fault (same family as H97; inverter not working properly). From what you have checked, this needs an appliance engineer to look at it: the next steps are beyond the checks that are safe to do yourself.\n[Safety panel] Don't remove the microwave's casing or try to repair it inside. Parts inside a microwave can hold a dangerous electric charge even after it's unplugged — have it checked by a qualified engineer."
  }
 ],
